From 1cd2421a6f398b9705dc1ab5c1de2f9874ff1f25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:59:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Audio] What the user chose wins while its device is
 there, and its output stays lit for it

Issue #24, a report of 2026-11-26: an Intel board with an AV receiver on
its DisplayPort output and an RTX 3050 with the TV. The audio setting
named the Intel output ("HDA Intel PCH"), chosen when the TV was on that
output; the TV is on the NVIDIA card now and the receiver on the Intel
output, whose ELD names it ("PIO AV Receiver on DisplayPort #0"). Two
rules of 1.0 took that choice away:

- OutputForDisplayInUse() followed the display that the setting was
  chosen with to the output that has it now ("was chosen with the display
  GSM LG TV, which is on 'ALSA:hdmi:CARD=NVidia,DEV=0' now: using that
  output"), made for the NVIDIA and Intel drivers, which number their
  HDMI outputs in the order the displays came. It did so across cards,
  where the number is not the question: the receiver on the port the user
  chose lost its sound to the TV.
- The windowing system lights only the display in use: the receiver's
  output was turned off as an output that Kodi does not use, its ELD went
  away, and the Intel output lost its name in the list of the settings
  ("the Intel audio port option disappeared").

What the user chose now wins while its device is there:

- ActiveAEFollowDisplay.h: OutputForDisplayInUse() takes whether the
  setting is the user's (SoundDisplays::chosenByUser, ChosenByUser()),
  and whether the display it is kept with was kept when the user chose
  it (RememberedDisplay::chosen, a "+" before its text, new). For such a
  choice the display it was chosen with is followed wherever it is, also
  when it is not the display in use; the configured output with that
  display on it keeps the sound (USER_OUTPUT, where it is not the display
  in use). A device of its own on the configured output, while the
  display it was chosen with is on another card
  (ChosenPortHasItsOwnDevice()), keeps the configured output, also for a
  setting from before. Only where the user's device is on no output does
  the sound go to the display in use. Another number on the same card is
  still the same display followed. A display kept for a setting from
  before (the display its number had when it was first seen, which can be
  another one than the user chose: the session of 2026-11-12 kept the
  Odyssey for a setting chosen for the TV) and a setting that the user
  did not choose are decided as before, and kodi.log says that choosing
  the output again keeps its sound on it.
- RememberDisplays(): a display is kept as chosen where the user changed
  the setting from an output kept before; and a setting whose display
  went to another card while its own output has a device is kept with
  that device, as chosen (RelearnedDisplay(), CActiveAESink::
  OwnDeviceOfChosenPort()), and the log says so.
- PublishSoundOutputs(): an output whose display is the device of a
  setting the user chose, kept as chosen, is marked SoundOutput::keepLit,
  and
  KEEP_OUTPUTS::OutputsForSound() keeps the graphics output that is
  certain to carry it lit, whatever "Keep the display of the audio output
  on" says, as an output that hades-keep-outputs keeps on. What is not
  certain keeps only the output with the picture, as before.
- kodi.log says each decision: the output kept for the user's device
  that is not the display in use, the setting kept with a new device,
  the output of the display in use taken while the user's device is
  there no more, and the outputs lit for a device the user chose.
- The help of "Keep the display of the audio output on" says what it
  still does: it keeps the chosen output, and its display on, also while
  its device is off or not there (en_gb, es_es, es_ar, es_mx).

TestActiveAEFollowDisplay: the outputs of the PC of issue #24 (the audio
setting keeps the receiver, the passthrough setting the TV, a device
that is not there, the same display under another number of one card,
a receiver chosen on its own output, the port judged only where its card
is known, the setting of the session of 2026-11-12 kept with a monitor
before, the "+" of a display kept as chosen). TestActiveAEKeptOutputs: the receiver's output lit for the
user's choice with the setting off, not for a sound that is not certain
or not chosen.
